 "note": "Unemployment, national income and retail sales for the four markets, built to the same convention as macro.json and macro_fiscal.json: a source name, a source_url, an api_url, the indicator code and a source_last_updated per block, with the period each figure covers. It is a SIBLING file: macro.json, macro_fiscal.json, macro_rates.json and macro_tax.json are left byte-identical. A national labour-force survey and an ILO-modelled estimate are different measures and are never merged: both are carried, each labelled with its basis. Nothing here was estimated or interpolated and no value was carried from another year: a figure is either the value the source publishes for that exact period, a figure quoted verbatim from a fetched source document, or an explicit not_published state with the reason.",
